      "final_text": "Done. `tools/minidiff.py` is a dependency-free Python 3 CLI (standard library only: `difflib`, `re`, `sys`) that diffs two files at line level, then re-diffs each changed line pair at word level so the specific substituted words are marked: removals as `[-word-]`, additions as `{+word+}`. It prints only changed hunks with 1 line of context and exits 1 on differences, 0 when identical.\n\n**One bug found and fixed.** My first version always wrote the two-number form in hunk headers (`@@ -6,2 +6,1 @@`). Unified diff format omits the length when a range covers exactly one line, so the correct header is `@@ -6,2 +6 @@`. I added a `format_range` helper and re-verified.\n\n**Verification performed:**\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Hunk headers vs system `diff -U1`, 5 file pairs | all match, including single-line and empty-file ranges |\n| Full output vs `diff -U1` body, word markers stripped | byte-identical |\n| All 3 substituted words present | `granite`, `sixty`, `bell` each found |\n| Exit code, files differ | 1 |\n| Exit code, identical files | 0 |\n| Bad argument count / unreadable file | usage or error on stderr, exit 2 |\n\nThe three substitutions are `rocky`\u2192`granite` (line 1), `forty`\u2192`sixty` (line 3), and `horn`\u2192`bell` (line 5). Lines 2 and 4 are unchanged and appear only as context. No browser verification applies here, since this is a command-line tool with no web surface.\n\nExact diff output between `a.txt` and `b.txt` (exit code 1):\n\n```text\n@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@\n-The lighthouse stood alone on the [-rocky-] headland.\n+The lighthouse stood alone on the {+granite+} headland.\n Every night its lamp swept a slow arc across the water.\n-Fishermen steered by that pale beam for [-forty-] years.\n+Fishermen steered by that pale beam for {+sixty+} years.\n The keeper climbed the spiral stairs at dusk without fail.\n-When the fog rolled in, the [-horn-] answered the darkness.\n+When the fog rolled in, the {+bell+} answered the darkness.\n```"
